<title>USA: U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 6.460 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 6.460 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 2-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 2-YEAR NOTES DUE APRIL 30, 1999</p>
<p>			     $17.009 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	6.460    Awarded At	99.843	6.375</p>
<p> MEDIAN    6.445    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 6.400    49 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.43 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 30.Apr.99</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    2-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 30.Apr.97</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 22.Apr.97</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  17.009 BLN USD		 CUSIP   9128272R2</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   41.366			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE    1.312				DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 6.375</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN   1.300			   PRICE	 99.843</p>
